    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No worries, I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Think of it like a clever little trap, where the funds are held until the right moment to spring into action.\n\nIn Toronto, the escrow account is typically managed by a third-party escrow agent, such as a bank or a specialized escrow company. They're like the goblin's trusted lieutenant, handling the day-to-day operations and ensuring that the funds are released only when the conditions are met.\n\nThe realtor usually sets up the escrow account and coordinates with the escrow agent, but they don't typically manage the funds themselves. It's a bit like how a goblin might have a trusted accomplice to help with the treasure counting – the realtor acts as the liaison, while the escrow agent handles the actual funds.\n\nIn some cases, the bank that's financing the mortgage might also be involved in managing the escrow account, especially if they're handling the loan. But in general, the escrow agent is the one responsible for holding the funds and ensuring that the transaction is completed smoothly.",
